From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:59:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2request: hevc: take the one-buffer SAND for 8-bit
 output

rpi-hevc-dec lists NV12MT_COL128 (luma and chroma in two buffers) before
NV12_COL128 (one buffer, the chroma of each 128-byte column after its
luma), and the destination format callback takes the first SAND format
it is offered, so 8-bit frames come out in two dmabufs.

A consumer that imports the frame into GL as one dmabuf cannot use that.
qemu's virtio-media decoder does exactly that to hand hardware frames to
a guest without a pass over the pixels on the CPU, and its import takes
one buffer with the chroma at an offset, the layout bcm2835-codec
produces.

Refuse the two-buffer form for 8 bit, so NV12_COL128 is chosen. The
frame descriptor then has one object and two planes. 10 bit is
unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_request_hevc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_request_hevc.c
@@ -151,10 +151,15 @@ static int dst_fmt_accept_cb(void * v, const struct v4l2_fmtdesc *fmtdesc)
 
     // SAND is currently confised as to whether it is s/w or hardware
     // *** Current usage is probably wrong - it shouldn't be a h/w fmt
-    if (fmtdesc->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128 ||
-        fmtdesc->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128M) {
+    // 8 bit: the one-buffer form only. A consumer that imports the frame
+    // as one dmabuf (qemu's virtio-media decoder, into GL) cannot take the
+    // two-buffer NV12MT_COL128, which rpi-hevc-dec lists first.
+    if (fmtdesc->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128) {
         return bit_depth == 8;
     }
+    if (fmtdesc->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128M) {
+        return 0;
+    }
     if (fmtdesc->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128 ||
         fmtdesc->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128M) {
         return bit_depth == 10;
